# Empirical Dehydration Study Dataset

## Overview
This dataset contains time-series physiological data gathered across a 3-hour fluid restriction protocol on 30 participants to determine algorithmic weighting for the Dehydration Hazard Index (DHI)[cite: 1].

## Dataset Columns

| Column Name | Data Type | Units | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `Participant_ID` | String | — | Unique identifier for each participant (`P01`–`P12`, etc.)[cite: 1] |
| `Timepoint` | String | — | Test phase (`Baseline`, `1_Hour`, `2_Hours`, `3_Hours`)[cite: 1] |
| `Duration_Hours` | Integer | Hours | Elapsed time in dehydration trial ($0, 1, 2, 3$)[cite: 1] |
| `Skin_Conductance_uS` | Float | $\mu\text{S}$ | Electrodermal skin conductance measured via GSR[cite: 1] |
| `Skin_Temperature_C` | Float | °C | Surface skin temperature recorded via DS18B20 probe[cite: 1] |
| `Heart_Rate_BPM` | Integer | BPM | Pulse rate extracted from PPG signal[cite: 1] |

## Data Collection Context & Disclaimer
* **Academic Setting**: Collected as part of an undergraduate Level 4, Term II (4-2) academic coursework project in Biomedical Engineering at CUET[cite: 1].
* **Exploratory Status**: Readings were recorded under prototype laboratory testing conditions without clinical reference standards (such as blood osmolarity or urine specific gravity)[cite: 1].
* **Purpose**: Calibration and validation of relative sensor fusion dynamics only[cite: 1].
